{"game": "arma-3", "language": "english", "appid": 107410, "month": "2018-08", "window": 4, "start_date": 1535068800, "end_date": 1535759999, "month_true_total": 398, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-10-09 11:08:52 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "44497739", "author": {"steamid": "76561198119493559", "personaname": "Gecko551", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/Gecko551/", "num_games_owned": 222, "num_reviews": 7, "playtime_forever": 212394, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 35342, "last_played": 1788976949, "avatar": "20260325269428aa1ed61f7c33ede35038c79a48"}, "language": "english", "review": "ArmA 3 is, in my opinion, an extremely good game. It depicts modern ground and air based battle very realisticly while still keeping the experience enjoyable (experience can be varied between more arcade like gameplay and full on military simulation mainly by changing the HUD). The multiplayer (especially the gamemode \"Zeus\") can be very fun ,with a few friends, however i would recommend to play at least a part of the, sadly only mediocre, campaign to get used to gameplay, tactics and controls and also to have a general understanding of all the aspects of the game including infantry, armored vehicle, unmanned vehicle and aircraft operation. The expansive modding community only serves to add to the experience as it adds everything from WWII equipment to equipment from other franchises like HALO to the game if one downloads and activates the mods in the very easily usable launcher. In conclusion I cannot recommend this game enough to anyone who i interested in semi to fully realistic military simulation and find fun in tactical and easy-to-learn-hard-to-master games.", "timestamp_created": 1535759732, "timestamp_updated": 1711140775, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 2, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.52702707052230835", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false,